{"name":"Elite Green","hex":"#133700","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of high birth or social position; aristocratic or patrician.","Representing the choicest or most select of a group."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A special group or social class of people who have a superior social or economic status and attendant power, advantages, or privileges in society; a member of such a group.","An individual member of such a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elite"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elite","blocks":[{"text":"In political and sociological theory, the elite are a small group of powerful or wealthy people who hold a disproportionate amount of wealth, privilege, political power, or skill in a group. Defined by the Cambridge Dictionary, the \"elite\" are \"the richest, most powerful, best-educated, or best-trained group in a society\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg/330px-Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elite","wikidata":"Q192797"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/500px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/1280px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/500px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bill Clinton (left middle),[21][22] Jeffrey Epstein (right middle),[21][22][23][24] and Ghislaine Maxwell (right)[21] have been characterized as associating with the global elite.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Demo-gegen-wef.jpg/500px-Demo-gegen-wef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail